The others have already pointed out the difference between cursed and
non-cursed scrolls of confuse monster..
But just one more thing: you seem to confuse scrolls, spells and wands and
whatever.. they are all different things.

Scrolls: You just read them. And whatever they do, they do immediately.
You don't zap, apply or do anything else like that to them. (OK, there is
one scroll that is best used by putting it on the floor and standing on
it.)

Spellbooks: You read them to learn the spell. There is no other immediate
effect but you can see the spell added to the known spells list with the
'+' command. And you cast the spell from that list with the 'Z' command.

Wands: You zap them with the 'z' command. And you can also apply a wand
with the 'a' command to break it. If the wand isn't empty, the effect is
something close to the zapping effect of the same wand.

There are many cases where casting some spell and zapping some wand has a
similar or almost similar effect. And some cases where castting some spell
and reading some scroll has similar effect, but they are still different
things, used with different commands.

